    "body": "## Purpose\n\nOn ROCm, `_supports_native_decode` is `next_n in (1, 2)`, so MTP with 2+ speculative tokens is flattened to one row per draft token and each row re-reads its sequence's KV. The AITER paged kernels have no such limit. This adds `VLLM_ROCM_INDEXER_NATIVE_DECODE_MAX_NEXT_N` (default 2, today's behaviour) to raise the cap.\n\n**Needs #59420** above `next_n = 2` (otherwise `Memory access fault` in warm-up).\n\n## Test Plan\n\nGLM-5.3, TP4, MI355X, `deepseek_mtp`, cap = 8, Gluon decode, #59420 applied, CUDA graphs on. Throughput sweep, GPQA Diamond, RULER niah_single_2 (64k).\n\n## Test Result\n\n| next_n (spec tokens) | GPQA | NIAH | Geomean tok/s/GPU |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| no MTP | 0.879 | 1.00 | 2435.5 |\n| 3 (2) | 0.889 | 1.00 | 3309.1 |\n| 5 (4) | 0.904 | 1.00 | 3607.8 |\n\nThroughput per GPU:\n\n| Conc | 8k/1k no MTP | 8k/1k n=3 | 8k/1k n=5 | 60k/600 no MTP | 60k/600 n=3 | 60k/600 n=5 |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 4 | 544.4 | 1105.3 | 1337.0 | 2925.1 | 4067.3 | 4422.3 |\n| 8 | 897.5 | 1650.6 | 2015.3 | 3889.2 | 4658.8 | 4408.6 |\n| 16 | 1415.4 | 2177.6 | 2648.5 | 4550.6 | 4948.6 | 5050.4 |\n| 32 | 2058.7 | 3061.8 | 3638.4 | 4938.2 | 5175.0 | 5303.4 |\n| 64 | 2853.3 | 4013.9 | 4447.8 | | | |\n| 128 | 3741.3 | 4715.5 | 4291.3 | | | |\n| 256 | 4603.2 | 4663.6 | 5208.6 | | | |\n\nThe no-MTP run is the same setup without speculative decoding (decode paged MQA logits on the FlyDSL kernel instead of Gluon).\n",
